    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24733" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inversĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		inverto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>an inversion.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Verborum, i. e. <i>an ironical inversion of meaning</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or.
				2, 65</span></i>. 261.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An allegory</i>, transl. of Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλληγορία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">Quint. 8,
				6, 44</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A transposition</i>, i. q. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναστροφή</span> (as quoque ego for ego quoque), <i><span class="en">Quint. 1,
				5, 40</span></i>.</div>
